<%# The geo manager's lab page.

    Two renders BY NAME, and nothing else: the badge a host puts in its navbar,
    and the engine's own /admin/geo template. Everything the specs drive — the
    squares' paint, the summary chips, the tabs, the live preview — belongs to
    those two files. A lab page that hand-rolled any of it would grade itself.

    The badge is given the SAME location the controller reports as this visitor's
    (US-CO), because that pairing is the preview's whole subject: the script
    repaints the badge showing where you are, and leaves any other badge alone. %>
<main class="p-8">
  <p data-test="lab-body">geo settings lab</p>

  <nav class="mb-6">
    <%= render "components/geo_badge",
          subdivision: E2eLabController::LAB_SUBDIVISION,
          country: E2eLabController::LAB_COUNTRY,
          blocked: false,
          simulated: false %>
  </nav>

  <%= render template: "studio/geo_settings/edit" %>
</main>
